      "@id": "kt:shareholder-primacy",
      "@type": "kto:Theory",
      "skos:prefLabel": "Shareholder Primacy: The Corporate Objective of Maximizing Shareholder Value",
      "skos:definition": "The view that a business corporation exists chiefly to serve its shareholders, so that directors and managers should run it to maximize shareholder wealth, typically measured as long-run firm or share value, within the law.",
