    {
      "@id": "kt:eighty-twenty-rule",
      "@type": "kto:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "80/20 Rule",
      "skos:definition": "The heuristic that, in many populations of causes, a small share of items accounts for most of the effect (conventionally 20% producing 80%), named by Joseph Juran after Vilfredo Pareto's observations on wealth and used to focus analysis and improvement on the \"vital few\".",
