      "@id": "kt:arbitrage",
      "@type": "kto:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "Arbitrage",
      "skos:definition": "The simultaneous purchase and sale of the same or equivalent assets in different markets or forms to profit from a price difference; in finance theory, the assumption that such riskless profits cannot persist underpins valuation results from the Modigliani-Miller theorem to option pricing.",
