      "skos:prefLabel": "Efficient Market Hypothesis",
      "skos:definition": "The theory, formalized by Eugene Fama in 1970, that security prices fully reflect available information, so investors cannot systematically earn above-normal risk-adjusted returns by trading on that information; it is usually tested in weak, semi-strong and strong forms.",
