    {
      "@id": "kt:michael-c-jensen",
      "@type": "kto:Person",
      "skos:prefLabel": "Michael Jensen",
      "skos:definition": "American financial economist (1939–2024) at the University of Rochester and Harvard Business School who co-authored the 1976 agency-cost theory of the firm with William Meckling, introduced Jensen's alpha for fund performance, founded the Journal of Financial Economics and co-founded SSRN; his ideas shaped equity-based executive pay, leveraged buyouts and the shareholder-value movement.",
