      "@id": "kt:small-business-set-asides",
      "@type": "kto:Practice",
      "skos:prefLabel": "Small Business Set-Asides: Reserving Federal Contracts for Small Firms",
      "skos:definition": "A US federal procurement preference in which an agency limits competition for a contract, or part of one, to small businesses, triggered mainly by the \"rule of two\": a reasonable expectation of offers from at least two responsible small firms at fair market prices.",
