    {
      "@id": "kt:open-innovation",
      "@type": "kto:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "Open Innovation: Purposive Inflows and Outflows of Knowledge",
      "skos:definition": "An approach to innovation, articulated by Henry Chesbrough in 2003, in which a firm deliberately brings outside ideas and technologies into its innovation process and sends unused internal ideas out to the market through others, instead of relying only on its own R&D and its own paths to market.",
