      "skos:prefLabel": "Management by Objectives: Goal-Setting Through Superior-Subordinate Agreement",
      "skos:definition": "A management practice, first outlined by Peter Drucker in The Practice of Management (1954), in which managers and subordinates jointly agree on results-focused objectives aligned with organizational goals, plan how to reach them, monitor their own progress and review performance against those objectives.",
