      "skos:prefLabel": "Principal-Agent Problem",
      "skos:definition": "The incentive problem that arises when one party (the principal) relies on another (the agent) to act on its behalf but cannot fully observe the agent's actions or information, so the principal must design a contract that trades off motivating the agent against the cost of loading risk onto them.",
