      "skos:prefLabel": "Gaps Model of Service Quality",
      "skos:definition": "A diagnostic framework, introduced by Parasuraman, Zeithaml and Berry in 1985, that explains a shortfall in perceived service quality (the customer gap between expected and perceived service) as the result of four gaps inside the provider: knowledge, standards, delivery and communication.",
