      "@id": "kt:devils-advocacy",
      "@type": "kto:Practice",
      "skos:prefLabel": "Devil's Advocate Method",
      "skos:definition": "A structured group decision technique in which one member or subgroup is assigned to critique a proposed plan, its assumptions and its evidence, so that flaws surface before the group commits; studied since the 1970s-80s as a counter to groupthink and compared with dialectical inquiry and consensus.",
