      "skos:prefLabel": "Dynamic Capabilities",
      "skos:definition": "A strategy theory holding that durable competitive advantage in fast-changing markets comes from a firm's ability to integrate, build and reconfigure its resources and competences, usually described as sensing opportunities, seizing them and transforming the organization.",
