      "@id": "kt:switching-costs",
      "@type": "kto:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "Consumer Switching Costs",
      "skos:definition": "The one-time costs a buyer incurs when moving from its current supplier to a rival, such as learning, set-up, contractual penalties or lost relationships; they lock customers in, shape \"bargain-then-ripoff\" pricing and act as a barrier to entry and a source of supplier power.",
